  "tactics": {
    "styleTags": [
      "Organized",
      "High press",
      "Counter-attack",
      "Physical"
    ],
    "tacticalNote": "Ouahbi's Morocco inherited Regragui's defensive blueprint and has maintained it. They sit in a compact structure, invite the opposition forward, then win the ball with aggressive pressing and explode into transition through Hakimi on the right and Ben Seghir cutting inside. The back four is disciplined. Set pieces are carefully rehearsed.",
    "strength": "Defensive compactness and collective pressing intensity — Morocco held elite teams scoreless in 2022 with this approach, making them one of the hardest teams to break down.",
    "vulnerability": "Replacing Ziyech's creativity is the open question — Ben Seghir is the heir but has far less tournament experience, and Morocco can look blunt in attack when the press fails."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "Hakimi's overlapping runs — he bombs forward from right-back with the timing and directness of a winger, creating overloads repeatedly.",
    "Morocco's press triggers — Regragui has specific patterns for when and how the collective press kicks in. One player presses, the whole shape shifts.",
    "Bounou's distribution: he starts Morocco's attacks with quick throws and passes rather than long balls, enabling the press to stay high."
  ],
